CD        CD [drive:][path] - Show or change the current directory.
COPY      COPY source [destination] [/Y | /-Y] - COPYCMD presets overwrite behavior. The last explicit overwrite switch wins.
DEL       DEL [drive:][path]filename [/P] [/Q] - /Q skips bulk confirmation and /P prompts for each file.
DELTREE   DELTREE [/Y] path [path...] - Delete a directory tree. /Y skips confirmation.
DIR       DIR [path] [/A[:attrs]] [/B] [/L] [/O[:order]] [/P] [/S] [/W] - DIRCMD sets defaults. /- cancels a preset switch.
FORMAT    FORMAT drive: [options] - /Q performs a quick format.
HELP      HELP [command] - List topics or display a command summary. Use HELP | MORE to page.
MD        MD [drive:]path - Create a directory.
MEM       MEM [/C | /CLASSIFY | /D | /DEBUG] [/P] - Show memory usage, optionally with paging.
MORE      MORE [filename] - Page a text file or piped input.
MOVE      MOVE [/Y | /-Y] source[,source...] destination - Move files or rename a directory. /-Y asks before overwriting.
RD        RD [drive:]path - Remove an empty directory.
REN       REN [drive:][path]oldname newname - Rename files.
TYPE      TYPE [drive:][path]filename - Display a text file.
XCOPY     XCOPY source [destination] [options] - /S includes subdirectories and /E includes empty ones with /S. XCOPYCMD sets defaults. /-S and /-E cancel those presets.
CHDIR     CD [drive:][path] - Show or change the current directory.
ERASE     Alias for DEL. /Q skips bulk confirmation and /P prompts for each file.
MKDIR     MD [drive:]path - Create a directory.
RMDIR     RD [drive:]path - Remove an empty directory.
RENAME    REN [drive:][path]oldname newname - Rename files.
/?        HELP [command] - List topics or display a command summary. Use HELP | MORE to page.

CONFIG.SYS drivers and support files
ANSI.SYS     DEVICE=ANSI.SYS - Add ANSI console escape-sequence support.
DISPLAY.SYS  Load with DEVICE= to configure display code-page support.
DRIVER.SYS   Load with DEVICE= to add a logical floppy drive.
EMM386.SYS   Expanded-memory driver for 386-class systems.
PRINTER.SYS  Load with DEVICE= to configure printer code-page support.
RAMDRIVE.SYS Load with DEVICE= to create a RAM disk.
SMARTDRV.SYS Load with DEVICE= to install the disk cache.
UMBS.SYS     DEVICE=UMBS.SYS start-end [...] - Supply mapped RAM as UMBs. Use hexadecimal segment addresses and exclusive end addresses.
VDISK.SYS    Load with DEVICE= to create a virtual disk in memory.
XMAEM.SYS    XMA emulation driver.
XMA2EMS.SYS  Provide EMS services using XMA memory.
COUNTRY.SYS  Country data selected by the CONFIG.SYS COUNTRY= directive.
KEYBOARD.SYS Keyboard layout data used by KEYB.

Additional commands
APPEND     Set the search path for data files.
ASSIGN     Redirect drive letters.
ATTRIB     Display or change file attributes.
BACKUP     Back up files for later use with RESTORE.
BREAK      BREAK [ON|OFF] - Control extended Ctrl+C checking.
CALL       CALL batchfile [arguments] - Run a nested batch file.
CHCP       CHCP [codepage] - Display or change the active code page.
CHKDSK     Check disk allocation and report errors.
CLS        Clear the display.
COMMAND    Start another command interpreter.
COMP       Compare files. /D shows decimal bytes, /A characters, /L line numbers, /N=n limits lines, /C ignores ASCII case.
CTTY       CTTY device - Change the command interpreter console.
DATE       DATE [date] - Display or set the date.
DEBUG      Inspect and modify memory and run machine-code programs.
DISKCOMP   Compare two floppy disks.
DISKCOPY   Copy a floppy disk. /V verifies destination tracks.
ECHO       ECHO [ON|OFF|message] - Control batch echoing or print a message.
EDLIN      Edit text one line at a time.
EXE2BIN    Convert an eligible EXE image to binary form.
EXIT       Leave the current command interpreter.
FASTOPEN   Cache information about frequently opened files.
FC         Compare files and report differences.
FDISK      Manage fixed-disk partitions. /STATUS reports disk usage and /MBR restores master boot code.
FIND       Search for text in files or input. /I ignores case.
FOR        Run a command for each item in a set.
GOTO       GOTO label - Continue a batch file at the named label.
GRAFTABL   Load an extended character table for graphics modes.
GRAPHICS   Enable graphics screen printing.
IF         Execute a batch command conditionally. IF [NOT] DIREXIST path command tests for a directory.
JOIN       Make a drive accessible through an existing directory.
KEYB       Configure the keyboard layout.
LABEL      Display, set, or remove a disk volume label.
LH         Run an external program in upper memory when available.
LOADFIX    LOADFIX program [arguments] - Run a program above the first 64 KiB.
LOADHIGH   Run an external program in upper memory when available.
MBASIC     Start the BASIC interpreter.
MODE       Configure a display or communications or printer device.
NLSFUNC    Load national-language support.
PATH       Display or set the executable search path.
PAUSE      Suspend batch execution until a key is pressed.
PRINT      Queue text files for background printing.
PROMPT     Change the command prompt.
RECOVER    Recover readable data from a file or disk.
REM        Add a comment to a batch file.
REPLACE    Replace files in a destination directory.
RESTORE    Restore BACKUP files. /D lists matching backup paths.
SELECT     Run the DOS setup utility.
SET        Display or change environment variables.
SHARE      Install file-sharing and locking support.
SHIFT      Shift the batch positional arguments.
SORT       Sort input lines.
SUBST      Associate a drive letter with a directory.
SYS        Transfer DOS system files to a disk.
TIME       TIME [time] - Display or set the time.
TREE       Display the directory tree.
TRUENAME   Display the canonical path for a file or directory.
VER        Display the DOS version.
VERIFY     VERIFY [ON|OFF] - Control verification of disk writes.
VI         Start the screen editor.
VOL        Display the disk volume label.

CONFIG.SYS directives
BREAK=     Enable or disable extended Ctrl+C checking.
BUFFERS=   Set the number of disk buffers.
COMMENT=   Change the CONFIG.SYS comment character.
COUNTRY=   Select country and code-page information.
CPSW=      Configure code-page switching.
DEVICE=    Load a device driver with optional arguments.
DEVICEHIGH= Try loading a driver in upper memory, with conventional memory as fallback.
DOS=       HIGH moves selected DOS routines into the HMA. UMB enables upper memory. Both can be combined.
DRIVPARM=  Override drive parameters. The geometry table supports format codes through /F:7.
FCBS=      FCBS=n,m sets the FCB count and protected count.
FILES=     Set the maximum number of open files.
INSTALL=   Run an executable during configuration.
LASTDRIVE= Set the highest drive letter.
MULTITRACK= Configure multitrack disk I/O.
SHELL=     Select the command interpreter and its arguments.
SHELLHIGH= Try placing the interpreter and permanent environment in upper memory.
STACKS=    STACKS=n,size sets the number and size of interrupt stacks.
SWITCHES=  /K selects conventional keyboard handling.
